# Latest dependencies

Direct dependencies live only in `requirements.txt`. Today those are `requests` and `pywebview`.

- When adding or changing a package, check PyPI and require at least the current release: `package>=X.Y.Z`.
- Do not pin an older release. Do not add an upper bound.
- Hold a newer release only when it breaks the 64-bit Windows WebView2 window, needs a Python other than the tablet’s 64-bit 3.13, or breaks the AxeOS calls this app makes.
- A newer pywebview does not change the 64-bit interpreter requirement. Do not move the window onto ARM64 Python.
- Leave transitive packages (`pythonnet`, `urllib3`, `certifi`, and the rest) to `requests` and `pywebview`. Do not add pywebview GUI extras (`gtk`, `qt`, `cef`).
